  "body": "## Associated User Story\n[P5-38 — Documentation and training](https://pt-502.atlassian.net/browse/P5-38)\n\nMembers and officers can find step-by-step app instructions, screenshots, troubleshooting, and practice exercises from Help. Officers have a separate system guide for installing and maintaining the app on Heroku.\n\n## Changes\n- Public member guide and officer-only app/system guides, with a sign-in help link and 15 screenshots using fictional training data.\n- Member training covers profiles, points and dues, calendars, location check-in, and outside-event submissions. Officer training covers member management, approvals, roles, event setup, QR codes, attendance, and point requirements.\n- One system guide works both offline and in the app. It covers organization ownership, local setup, Heroku deployment, initial manager setup, costs, backups, full database imports, failed import recovery, and compatible release rollback.\n- Added a Procfile and an initial-manager bootstrap task. Bootstrap preserves existing configuration and refuses to add a different manager when one already exists.\n- Added a guide maintenance checklist for future feature changes.\n\nSunny: A member opens Help before or after signing in and follows the current app steps. An officer can open both app training and the separate system guide.\n\nRainy: Anonymous and regular member requests to officer/system help are blocked. Troubleshooting explains sign-in, validation, location, submission, failed import, and deployment recovery steps.\n\n## Definition of Done\n### A — Review, standards, and setup\n- [ ] Code reviewed by a non-author before merge.\n- [x] Coding standard checked: RuboCop inspected 115 files with no offenses.\n- [x] Setup changes documented in README and the system guide.\n- CI results are available in this PR's Checks tab.\n\n### B — Human-only maintainability review\n- [ ] Reviewer checks meaningful names/comments, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, and Rails conventions.\n- [ ] Reviewer checks foreign keys, enums, and nested routes where applicable.\n\nThere are no model or schema changes. The help controller handles routing and access; guide navigation and screenshots use shared partials. The offline and in-app system guide use the same source file.\n\n### C — Tests\n- [x] Full RSpec suite: 321 examples, 0 failures, 1 existing pending example.\n- [x] Nine new examples cover help access, live guide links and anchors, screenshot assets, initial manager setup, and safe bootstrap retries.\n- [x] Rails loading check and Brakeman passed (0 security warnings).\n- [x] Production asset precompilation passed.\n- [x] Chrome checked the guides at desktop and 375-pixel phone width; no horizontal overflow on help pages.\n\n### D — Deferred items and exclusions\n- Non-author review and Section B remain pending for the team before merge.\n- Live Heroku provisioning, paid plan selection, database import/restore, and release rollback were not performed on a club account. The guide provides staging rehearsal and verification steps for the account owner.\n- The existing pending HomeHelper example is unchanged. No new RuboCop exclusions were added.\n- Documentation describes the currently merged app. The separate, unmerged Get Involved import work is not presented as an available CSV import feature.\n",
